From: helmfile-enhancement-plan
Subject: [PATCH] PR-T-10 — KEDA scaling validation (synthetic load -> assert HPA scaled)

Closes G10 (no assertion that KEDA actually scaled).
Branch: test/keda-scaling-validation-job
Depends-on: PR-HF-10 (KEDA fixed) and PR-T-08 (gRPC connectivity confirmed)

CRITICAL: this Job submits 200 workflows. Only enable in canary clusters
(label `gcp-kitt.atlassian.com/cluster-class=canary`). The nodeSelector
in the spec enforces this.

---
 atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/test-keda-scaling-validation-job.yaml | 79 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 79 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/test-keda-scaling-validation-job.yaml

diff --git a/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/test-keda-scaling-validation-job.yaml b/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/test-keda-scaling-validation-job.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ddddddd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/test-keda-scaling-validation-job.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# KEDA-scaling synthetic-load validation. CANARY ONLY.
+# Authored by helmfile_enhancement_plan/PR-T-10 (2026-05-11).
+#
+# What this asserts:
+#   1. Submit 200 workflows to the scraper task queue.
+#   2. Sleep 90 s for KEDA to react.
+#   3. kubectl get hpa keda-hpa-scraper-worker-scaler -o jsonpath replicas >= 2
+#   4. Otherwise FAIL.
+#
+# How to run:
+#   kubectl apply -f test-keda-scaling-validation-job.yaml
+#   kubectl wait --for=condition=complete --timeout=240s job/keda-scaling-validation -n dtaske
+#   kubectl logs -n dtaske job/keda-scaling-validation
+apiVersion: batch/v1
+kind: Job
+metadata:
+  name: keda-scaling-validation
+  namespace: dtaske
+  labels:
+    app.kubernetes.io/name: keda-scaling-validation
+    app.kubernetes.io/test-class: load
+    gcp-kitt.atlassian.com/canary-only: "true"
+spec:
+  backoffLimit: 1
+  activeDeadlineSeconds: 300
+  ttlSecondsAfterFinished: 600
+  template:
+    spec:
+      restartPolicy: Never
+      nodeSelector:
+        gcp-kitt.atlassian.com/cluster-class: canary   # safety: refuses to schedule outside canary
+      serviceAccountName: keda-scaling-validation-sa
+      containers:
+        - name: load
+          image: temporalio/admin-tools:1.28.1-tctl-1.18.4-cli-1.4.1
+          env:
+            - name: TEMPORAL_ADDRESS
+              value: temporal-frontend.temporal.svc.cluster.local:7233
+            - name: TASK_QUEUE
+              value: scraper
+          command: ["/bin/sh", "-c"]
+          args:
+            - |
+              set -euo pipefail
+              echo "[1/4] Submitting 200 workflows..."
+              for i in $(seq 1 200); do
+                tctl --address ${TEMPORAL_ADDRESS} workflow start \
+                  --workflow_id "load-test-${i}" \
+                  --workflow_type ScraperWorkflow \
+                  --tasklist ${TASK_QUEUE} \
+                  --execution_timeout 60 \
+                  --input '{"url":"https://example.com"}' >/dev/null
+              done
+              echo "[2/4] Sleeping 90s for KEDA to react..."
+              sleep 90
+              echo "[3/4] Inspecting HPA replicas..."
+              REPLICAS=$(kubectl get hpa keda-hpa-scraper-worker-scaler -n dtaske \
+                -o jsonpath='{.status.currentReplicas}' || echo 0)
+              echo "Current replicas: ${REPLICAS}"
+              echo "[4/4] Assertion..."
+              if [ "${REPLICAS}" -lt 2 ]; then
+                echo "FAIL: KEDA did not scale (replicas=${REPLICAS}); HPA frozen — see HF-10"
+                kubectl describe hpa keda-hpa-scraper-worker-scaler -n dtaske
+                exit 1
+              fi
+              echo "OK: KEDA scaled to ${REPLICAS} replicas"
+          resources:
+            requests:
+              cpu: 100m
+              memory: 128Mi
+            limits:
+              memory: 256Mi
+          securityContext:
+            runAsNonRoot: true
+            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
+            readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
+            capabilities:
+              drop: ["ALL"]
